<?nvs
// The load leg's case: the response has to name the request that asked for it.
//
// `hello.nvs` beside this one answers every request with the same bytes, which
// is right for the throughput comparison it serves and useless for the question
// `bun nv bench-load` asks — an answer delivered to the wrong connection is
// byte-identical to the right one, so no generator can tell the two apart. Here
// the body is the token the request carried and nothing else, and
// `nvs-serve-probe` checks every one of them.
//
// It has no `.php` twin on purpose: this leg has no second engine to agree
// with, so there is nothing for a twin to be. `hello.php` is the twin of
// `hello.nvs`, for the leg that does.
//
// The query is read rather than the path, because `rule:http-server/a-path-is-never-derived-from-a-url`
// means a per-request path would be a mount table this leg does not have.
echo "id=", Core\Request::query("n") as string, "\n";
